    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n@echasnovski I would prefer the default explorer navigation to `go_in` without opening the file buffer unless a different key map is pressed (example `L` or `CR`). Similar to most terminal file manager (example `yazi`).\r\n\r\nI am not very good at lua so I am not very sure how to write the tests but I tried to write it to my best ability. I did notice that `make test_files` on `main` branch was already failing. If someone could help update the tests it would be great!",
    "closed_at": "2024-11-07T13:27:16Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis is out of scope for 'mini.files' as too specialized and which I don't really support as a workflow. Also this can be done with custom buffer-local mappings (following [this example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8bc67a35e627908da644c5f8cd26b3f987f2627/doc/mini-files.txt#L445-L472)):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal go_in_if_dir = function()\r\n  if (MiniFiles.get_fs_entry() or {}).fs_type ~= 'directory' then return end\r\n  MiniFiles.go_in()\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\r\n  callback = function(args) vim.keymap.set('n', 'l', go_in_if_dir, { buffer = args.data.buf_id }) end,\r\n})\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup({ mappings = { go_in = '' } })\r\n```\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2024-11-07T13:27:16Z",
